From: Vorapol Rinsatitnon <vorapol.r@pm.me>
Date: Fri, 04 Sep 2026 20:04:27 +1200
Subject: [PATCH] cmd/go: restore GOPATH-mode go get

CL 518775 (Go 1.22) removed GOPATH-mode "go get".

	GO111MODULE=off go get  ->  cannot resolve an import path
	                        ->  cannot clone under GOPATH/src
	                        ->  cannot install the result

Restore it from the tree immediately before that change, together with the
prerequisites removed after it in the dead-code sweeps that followed.

Three things differ from the code at the removal point, where the tree has
since moved on.

	par.Cache.Clear    ->  uses sync.Map.Clear
	vcs.FromDir        ->  keeps the later nested-repository checks
	PackageError.Hard  ->  the branch reading it is dropped, not restored

Two scripts the removal deleted stay deleted. The GOPATH half of
get_insecure.txt is covered against the same host by get_insecure_env.txt and
get_insecure_custom_domain.txt, and the module half of get_404_meta.txt still
exercises the 404 path it was written for.


